# Input while an order's moves are shown (spec 06 §2.4 "Input", observed in the original) and
# the current sector after a move (§7 Q123, observed), on a training game of our own
# (tests/input/learn-moves): turn-based, two attack ships at home (sector 4,6).
# - A Move To given by a click on the map: until its moves are over, a key (F3) and a click on
#   a command button (Designs) do nothing, then or after. Once the ship has moved, the
#   top-left square is the current sector: no yellow marks anywhere, the ship's report still
#   open, its orders lit.
# - A Move To Waypoint given by its key (Ctrl+1, as its order button): a key gets through in the
#   middle of the moves: F3 opens Designs, and the moves stand still while it is open; closed,
#   they go on.
# - End Turn in the middle of such moves asks first, the moves standing still; Yes shows them at
#   once and ends the turn (the original fails there).
# - Nothing of a turn is drawn: right after the order the ship is still on its square.
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --learn-dir=tests/input/learn-moves --training=moves --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800

wait-lesson moves
wait 5
click tag:lesson:hide
# The slowest speed, so that each move lasts long enough to be caught in the middle.
key F2
wait-window game-menu
click item:Options in=game-menu
wait-window options
drag item:"Ship movement speed"@50%,50% in=options to item:"Ship movement speed"@1,50% in=options
key Escape
wait-closed options
# Waypoints 1 and 2, three and six squares north of home.
key Escape
wait 3
key Alt+1
wait-until { picking = "location" }
click sector:4,3
wait 3
key Alt+2
wait-until { picking = "location" }
click sector:4,0
wait 3

# The first ship: Move To five squares east, given by a click on the map.
click sector:home
wait-for item:report:ship
click item:report:ship nth=1
wait 2
assert-present sector:marked+home
key M
wait-until { picking = "move-to" }
click sector:9,6
# A new ship faces up: first a quarter turn, of which nothing is drawn.
assert-present sector:gliding+home
assert-present sector:marked+home
key F3
wait 2
click tag:command:designs
wait 3
assert-present sector:gliding
assert-no-window designs
wait-gone sector:gliding
wait 5
assert-no-window designs
# Moved: the top-left square is current, with no marks on it or anywhere; the report is the ship's.
assert-inside sector:selected sector:0,0
assert-absent sector:marked
assert-present item:Comps
assert { selected = "ship" }

# The second ship, still at home: Ctrl+1, Move To Waypoint 1 by its key, three squares north.
click sector:home
wait-for item:report:ship
click item:report:ship nth=1
wait 2
key Ctrl+1
wait 1
assert-present sector:gliding
# A key gets through: Designs opens, and the move stands still under it.
key F3
wait-window designs
wait 30
assert-present sector:gliding
screenshot held.png
key Escape
wait-closed designs
wait-gone sector:gliding
wait 3

# Waypoint 2 by its key, three squares more; End Turn in the middle asks, the move standing still.
key Ctrl+2
wait 1
assert-present sector:gliding
key F12
wait 20
assert-present sector:gliding
click item:Yes
wait 5
assert-absent sector:gliding
wait-turn 1
click tag:log:close optional
wait 3
